# Citation File Format 1.2.0
# https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# The single author entry is an institutional (entity) author. In CFF an author
# is an entity, rather than a person, when it carries "name" instead of
# "given-names" / "family-names". CFF 1.2.0 defines no "type" key on an author,
# so the institution is expressed in that entity form.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Turkish Citizenship by Investment: Open Data"
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable reference data on Turkiye's citizenship-by-investment
  programme: qualifying investment thresholds and their statutory basis, the
  conditions attached to each route, government and third-party transaction
  costs, the documents an application requires, published statistics on
  citizenship acquisitions and foreign property purchases, and an index of the
  primary sources behind each figure. Figures are dated and attributed to the
  instrument or publication they come from.
authors:
